# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend (Vite)
#
# ONLY these two. Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the JavaScript bundle
# at build time and shipped to every visitor — so a model API key here is a
# model API key published to the internet. That is not hypothetical: an earlier
# build of this project leaked a live Groq key exactly this way.
#
# The anon key belongs here and is safe here, because it grants nothing. RLS
# scopes every read to the signed-in owner, and no browser role holds a write
# grant on any table.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gateway edge function — set with `supabase secrets set`, never in this file
# on a deployed project, and never with a VITE_ prefix.
#
#   supabase secrets set GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
#   supabase secrets set ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://your-app.vercel.app
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected by the Supabase
# runtime — you do not set those yourself.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# External agent (agent/agent.mjs) — set in that machine's shell, not here
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HALT_GATEWAY_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co/functions/v1/gateway
# HALT_KEYFILE=./agent/agent.key.json
